in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled
in @code/mirror
in @code/gestalt

# @cascade/code/mirror/gestalt — the mirror substrate → gestalt IR
# value cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species
# shards group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source
# language (mirror substrate) groups together at
# `shards/cascade/code/mirror/`; target (gestalt IR here) leafs at
# `shards/cascade/code/mirror/gestalt.mirror`.
#
# THIS species is the FIRST LEG of the composition theorem chain
# per Alex 2026-08-03 verbatim:
#
#   *"Split cascade architecture: cascade<mirror, gestalt> +
#    cascade<gestalt, gleam> as separate species (not one combined
#    cascade). Opens door for cascade<gestalt, X> alternate
#    back-ends without touching mirror."*
#
# Composition-theorem chain per companion math 2026-08-03:
#
#   mirror substrate
#     ↓  @cascade/code/mirror/gestalt (THIS species)
#   gestalt IR (@code/gestalt AST + .gestalt file surface)
#     ↓  @cascade/code/gestalt/gleam (sibling mint this arc)
#   gestalt-ui-shaped Gleam
#     ↓  @cascade/code/gleam/js (landed sibling per Taut scout §5)
#   JS bundle
#     → browser peer runtime @peer/browser (mint this arc)
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The pattern of "cascade to gestalt IR" already appears at prose
# altitude in:
#
#   docs/scouts/2026-08-03-taut-distributed-colony-substrate-scout.md
#     §5 mint prerequisites — enumerated expected mint shape for
#     @cascade/code/mirror/gestalt per landed sibling template
#     (5 carriers + 3 actions + 4 sub-bilaterals + 1 composed
#     following @cascade/code/turing/mirror template).
#   docs/specs/2026-08-03-mara-distributed-colony-canonical-spec.md
#     — companion spec landing this arc; §Composition theorem names
#     this leg as required for chain closure.
#
# The sibling template @cascade/code/turing/mirror.mirror
# (`shards/cascade/code/turing/mirror.mirror`, 22.1KB, 2026-07-17)
# is the STRUCTURAL PRECEDENT — the reverse-direction cascade
# (tape → mirror substrate) that gives the shape mirror looks
# like at cascade altitude. This species mirrors that structure
# in the forward direction (mirror substrate → gestalt IR).
#
# === composition altitude: SUBSTRATE-NATIVE ↔ FILE-PROJECTION ===
#
# The source altitude is `@code/mirror` (shards/code/mirror.mirror
# 2026-06-07) — mirror's own instance of @code at the mirror
# altitude. The target altitude is `@code/gestalt` (shards/code/
# gestalt.mirror, this-arc landing) — the file-level projection
# of the @gestalt graph.
#
# THIS cascade is the AUTHOR-EMISSION edge: it emits `.gestalt`
# files that Alex (or Reed, or any peer) reads/writes in the
# register the corpus already carries. Per polyglot spec §3.2
# composition axiom, THIS species composes with:
#
#   - `@cascade/code/gestalt/gleam` (sibling mint this tick) →
#     gives the full mirror → gleam composition when chained.
#   - `@cascade/code/gleam/js` (landed) → chained further gives
#     mirror → js composition when the browser-peer target is
#     the final destination.
#   - Composable via `@glue.compose` with existing mirror substrate
#     carriers at their own altitudes.
#
# === The cascade shape (mirror substrate → gestalt IR) ===
#
# Source (mirror substrate admits per @code/mirror discipline):
# - substrate-decl graph (@mirror/store content-addressed refs)
# - composition edges (@glue.compose morphism composition)
# - typed carriers (@glass verdict + @nl language surface +
#   @prism five-op discipline)
# - substrate-native composition (@code/mirror grammar/render
#   sub-species)
# - identity-contract preservation (byte-equality on OID)
#
# Target (gestalt IR preserves per @code/gestalt + @gestalt):
# - .gestalt file structure (frontmatter + heading hierarchy +
#   line-break-as-structure per @code/gestalt/grammar)
# - @gestalt.gestalt_document (nodes + edges + annotations +
#   modes + visibility_scope)
# - register-honoring bytes (breath-marks + asymmetric brackets +
#   emoji + soft-breaks + corpus-links — ALL preserved verbatim)
# - round-trip identity (parse(render(doc)) = doc structurally)
#
# Per companion spec §4.4 (this cascade leg):
# - PRESERVED: substrate-decl semantics (every mirror shard-decl
#   has a .gestalt-file equivalent projection); OID content-address
#   (fragments preserve identity); the .gestalt corpus register
#   (per @code/gestalt/grammar 22 productions).
# - LOST: the substrate-decl's compile-time-only invariants that
#   have no reader-runtime discharge (e.g., mirror-substrate-only
#   bilateral verdict states); the substrate's parametricity
#   (labeled<v,m> collapses to raw refs at file altitude).
#
# The `loss_lens<@code/mirror, @code/gestalt>` measures these gaps
# against mirror's substrate-decl graph altitude + .gestalt's
# file-level projection altitude.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #95 (@cascade family-root; Mara canonical `ce4874b`,
#   2026-06-23): this species IS one of the cascade species
#   discharging the family-root.
# - Recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED (labeled<> functor at
#   `shards/labeled.mirror`): gestalt_ir_artifact uses labeled<>
#   instance for substrate-value + gestalt-projection-metadata.
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the
#   dimension-projection from mirror's substrate-decl-graph basis
#   to gestalt's file-projection basis IS measurable via
#   `measure_mirror_gestalt`; the projection REBASES mirror's
#   substrate-decl surface into gestalt's file-projection altitude
#   while preserving computational semantics.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Markdown → HTML          Gruber 2004 markdown.pl — first prose-
#                            to-web cascade with round-trip identity
#                            as design goal; ancestor of the
#                            register-preservation contract.
#   Wadler 2003             "A prettier printer" — the doc-combinator
#                            algebra @code/mirror.render + @code/
#                            gestalt.render both use; measurement of
#                            layout cost.
#   Bernardy 2017           "A pretty but not greedy printer" — the
#                            dynamic-programming optimality criterion
#                            over the doc algebra; grounds cascade
#                            emission of minimal-loss projections.
#   Reynolds 1983 + Wadler   Parametricity — the labeled<> functor
#     1989                   that lifts substrate-value refs with
#                            projection-metadata dimension.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/2026-08-03-mara-distributed-colony-
#               canonical-spec.md §Composition theorem + §Cascade
#               leg spec §mirror→gestalt.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (Alex
#                      2026-08-03 Q-C1 split-cascade directive),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (loss is @epistemologic/properties composite),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (every action
#                      body `\` blocked; FLOOR realization domain).
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (family-root),
#                 shards/labeled.mirror (functor primitive
#                                        gestalt_ir_artifact rests on),
#                 shards/code/mirror.mirror (source grammar),
#                 shards/code/gestalt.mirror (target grammar; this-arc
#                                             landing),
#                 shards/cascade/code/turing/mirror.mirror (structural
#                                                          precedent),
#                 shards/cascade/code/gestalt/gleam.mirror (sibling
#                                                           mint this
#                                                           arc; second
#                                                           cascade
#                                                           leg).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/mirror/gestalt.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/mirror/gestalt` per `@epistemologic/pact/
# path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/wadler-1989-theorems-for-free
source @arxiv/programming-languages/reynolds-1983-parametricity
source @arxiv/programming-languages/wadler-2003-prettier-printer
source @arxiv/programming-languages/bernardy-2017-pretty-not-greedy

prism @cascade/code/mirror/gestalt {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# === mirror_source carrier ===
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=mirror.
# References mirror-substrate content as the unit of cascade.
type mirror_source = ref

# === gestalt_projection_metadata carrier ===
# Structured carrier for the mirror-substrate → gestalt-IR
# projection shape (visibility_scope inference; annotation-carrier
# extraction; section-boundary detection from shard-decl grouping;
# emoji-carrier preservation).
type gestalt_projection_metadata = ref

# === gestalt_ir_artifact carrier ===
# The @labeled<> instance per recognition #93 H4. A gestalt_ir_
# artifact IS a gestalt-substrate-value ref annotated with
# gestalt_projection_metadata via the labeled functor.
type gestalt_ir_artifact = labeled(ref, gestalt_projection_metadata)

# === apply_mirror_gestalt action ===
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.compile for
# the mirror substrate → gestalt IR functor. Takes a mirror source
# ref; returns a gestalt IR ref (content-addressed per @mirror/store).
#
# The FLOOR resolver at [substrate-floor:@io-boundary] discharges
# via @code/mirror parsing + @code/gestalt emission per Wadler-
# Bernardy doc combinator algebra.
#
# requires mirror_source_well_formed(src, p): source must pass
# @code/mirror parsing per @code/mirror grammar discipline.
apply_mirror_gestalt(src: mirror_source, p: perturbation) -> ref
requires mirror_source_well_formed(src, p)
{ \ }

# === bundle_gestalt action ===
# Wraps a gestalt-IR ref + projection metadata into a gestalt_ir_
# artifact via @labeled.label construction.
bundle_gestalt(gestalt_ref: ref, metadata: gestalt_projection_metadata,
               p: perturbation) -> gestalt_ir_artifact
requires gestalt_projection_coherent(gestalt_ref, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_mirror_gestalt action ===
# Specialization of @cascade.measure for the mirror substrate →
# gestalt IR cascade. Returns imperfect<gestalt_ir_artifact, ref,
# information_loss> per @glass discipline.
measure_mirror_gestalt(src: mirror_source, artifact: gestalt_ir_artifact,
                        p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(gestalt_ir_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires mirror_gestalt_loss_well_defined(src, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === Sub-bilaterals ===

# mirror_source_well_formed — source-side well-formedness
bilateral mirror_source_well_formed {
  sentinel "mirror-source=parses-per-code-mirror-grammar"
  arity 1
}
mirror_source_well_formed(src: mirror_source, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# gestalt_projection_coherent — target-side well-formedness
bilateral gestalt_projection_coherent {
  sentinel "gestalt-projection=metadata-coherent-with-value"
  arity 2
}
gestalt_projection_coherent(gestalt_ref: ref,
                             metadata: gestalt_projection_metadata,
                             p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# mirror_gestalt_loss_well_defined — loss-measurability bilateral
bilateral mirror_gestalt_loss_well_defined {
  sentinel "cascade=source-artifact-pair-discharge-witnessed"
  arity 2
}
mirror_gestalt_loss_well_defined(src: mirror_source,
                                   artifact: gestalt_ir_artifact,
                                   p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# cascade_mirror_gestalt_admissible — @glue.compose admissibility
bilateral cascade_mirror_gestalt_admissible {
  sentinel "cascade=gestalt-substrate-consumable"
  arity 1
}
cascade_mirror_gestalt_admissible(cascade_outcome: gestalt_ir_artifact)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === Composed bilateral ===
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral for THIS species.
bilateral mirror_gestalt_cascade_well_formed {
  sentinel "cascade=all-sub-bilaterals-discharge"
  arity 2
}
mirror_gestalt_cascade_well_formed(src: mirror_source,
                                     artifact: gestalt_ir_artifact,
                                     p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires mirror_source_well_formed(src, p)
requires gestalt_projection_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires mirror_gestalt_loss_well_defined(src, artifact, p)
requires cascade_mirror_gestalt_admissible(artifact)
{ \ }

out @cascade/code/mirror/gestalt
out mirror_source
out gestalt_projection_metadata
out gestalt_ir_artifact
out apply_mirror_gestalt
out bundle_gestalt
out measure_mirror_gestalt
out mirror_source_well_formed
out gestalt_projection_coherent
out mirror_gestalt_loss_well_defined
out cascade_mirror_gestalt_admissible
out mirror_gestalt_cascade_well_formed
